════════════════════ step4_gevrey ════════════════════
Gevrey-k <-> essential singularity e^{-1/x^{1/(k)}} dictionary (standard):
  series sum a_n x^n with a_n ~ (k n)! has Borel-k summable structure,
  non-perturbative partner ~ exp(-const / x^{1/k}).

TARGET sigma_req: e^{-zeta u^{-1/4}}  => essential sing of order 1/4 in u
  => its perturbative partner (in u) would need a_n ~ (4n)! growth.
  (the '4' is the FOURTH-root order; this is the structural fingerprint.)

FREE thermal series: a_{2j} ~ Gamma-free, ~ (2j+1)/pi^{2j} = GEOMETRIC x linear.
  In worldline TIME tau the free series is CONVERGENT (radius 2pi/kappa);
  the (2n)! shows up only after Borel/Laplace to FREQUENCY -- a SIMPLE pole tower.

Growth-rate comparison of |a_n|^{1/n} normalized (the Gevrey order):
 n   (4n)!^{1/n}/n   (2n)!^{1/n}/n   free_a_n^{1/n} (->1/pi, bounded)
   5   951.1629         4.1019         0.344876
  10   6182.5054         6.8962         0.342214
  20   43823.4324         12.4323         0.335612
  40   327172.2153         23.4050         0.329640
  80   2517556.4884         45.2198         0.325319

=> (4n)! and (2n)! both DIVERGE as n->inf (Gevrey>0); free stays BOUNDED at 1/pi
   (Gevrey-0 / analytic in tau). The free WORLDLINE series is convergent.
   Neither (4n)! NOR (2n)! growth is present in the free tau-series coefficients.

